{#
	Error page art

	The fun element on the 404/403/500 pages, shared by all three so the joke is
	identical everywhere: a cave in ASCII — stalactites, a drip, a stick figure
	standing in the water, a stalagmite, and the author's commentary. The status
	code is deliberately *not* in the art, because this file is shared with the
	403 and the 500; each template renders its own as the bouncing
	`.error-code`.

	Why not a picture: the error pages deliberately carry no photo. The club
	masthead photo and the static caving banner are both real cave shots, and
	hanging one behind "your page is missing" turns the joke into advertising.
	`error-masthead` (styles.css) replaces the background image with a plain
	gradient.

	The same drawing is printed to the devtools console by scripts.js, which
	reads it back out of this element rather than keeping a second copy — so
	this file is the only place the art exists. Change it here and both places
	change at once.

	Spacing: spaces only, never tabs — a tab in a <pre> renders at the font's tab
	width rather than 8 and shears the drawing apart. Trailing whitespace has
	been stripped; it is invisible and it only makes the next edit's diff lie
	about what changed.
#}
